nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+3{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-2{C}_{2}.$"} {:db/id 17592186265946 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "958cdcf3-aaba-5275-85f8-9531f10b3d0e" :knowledge-point/title "Using Column Operations to Create a Row of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "266fdd0f-5ad2-54f6-9ca4-7015ec267b81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-3{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{3}$" :db/id 17592186263333} {:answer/id #uuid "3a1eec8f-4d09-5228-a74b-ee3c184432ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+3{C}_{3}$" :db/id 17592186263519} {:answer/id #uuid "6de5f574-c9ce-550b-86f8-bf53d48c91b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-3{C}_{3}$" :db/id 17592186263951} {:answer/id #uuid "aefa64aa-83e0-5872-9f90-8e5806976abf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+3{C}_{3}$" :db/id 17592186264508} {:answer/id #uuid "be13c6bc-a32a-543a-8a1f-5cbcb048c2ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-3{C}_{3}$" :db/id 17592186264652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aefa64aa-83e0-5872-9f90-8e5806976abf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+3{C}_{3}$" :db/id 17592186264508} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d91c8d4-2174-557a-bacf-309af204fdc1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186265360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2ce8c9c4-6db5-5686-9935-94470a40d94f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130627" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 5 & 6 & -9 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 2 & -6 \\\\ -7 & 2 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & -7 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary column operations \n\n- ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-3{C}_{3}$\n- ${C}_{2}:=…$\n- ${C}_{4}:=…$\n\neach of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{23}=2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 5 & 6 & -9 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 2 & -6 \\\\ -7 & 2 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}: &={C}_{1}-3{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 5 & 6 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}: &={C}_{2}-2{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & -7 & 6 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{4}: &={C}_{4}+3{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & -7 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1 & 11\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+3{C}_{3}.$"} {:db/id 17592186329696 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "958cdcf3-aaba-5275-85f8-9531f10b3d0e" :knowledge-point/title "Using Column Operations to Create a Row of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "104fe33f-70c8-5ff5-a1e2-9d744cc2efec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/va